From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:16:19 -0400
Subject: tabs: sleep, rename, row numbers, the selection rule, the short menu

Cmd-1..9 and Close Others / Clear Below skip the rows the user cannot see
(docs/features/tabs.md R10, menus M5); the tab-group chords are gone with
the rows they served (M6). A sleeping row is dimmed instead of ringed, and
'Sleep Tab' / 'Sleep Other Tabs in This Space' are verbs on the menu (R4, R5);
a Space the user left sleeps after the setting's minutes, essentials excepted
(R6, R8). A tab can be renamed in place: double-click, the menu's Rename...,
the name lives on the WebContents, is preferred by TabUIHelper, read by the
command bar, written as session extra data and re-emitted on rebuild
(R14-R17). Holding Cmd shows the row numbers in the close slot, as a corner
badge on cards and the rail, and Ctrl-N on the Space chips (R11-R13, R19).
Verbs act on the selection with plural labels (R20-R22). The tab menu is
Stedding's short one, verbs first, with Chromium's menu behind a setting
(menus M1, M4).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 2 (R6-13, R6-14, R6-15, R6-17, R6-20), the
sidebar behaviours Arc users expect from rows.
Removable when: Chromium's vertical tabs sleep, rename and number their rows
and let a menu be reordered without a fork.
